	affiliations = {Dept. of Computer Science & Engineering, Poornima University, Jaipur, India},
	abstract = {Sentiment analysis (SA), also known as opinion mining, is a method of analyzing the natural language used to gain information that is positive, negative or neutral and that appreciates the meaning inferred of view shared in web materials by users, entrepreneurs, or other owners. Researchers have recognized that the textual content aspect is not sufficient, so Aspect Based Sentiment Analysis (ABSA) has been created to capture the nature of the aspects expressed in the course of a particular study. A review of ABSA's most current state-of-the-art reveals a tremendous increase in identifying both aspect and sentiment. The dataset, domain, and reported performance are all presented for each mentioned study, as well as the aspect extraction method and sentiment prediction approach. The main purpose of this study is to provide a quick overview of ABSA methodologies. Here several approaches are discussed that focused on machine learning (ML), deep learning (DL) techniques and transfer leaning (TL) techniques. These approaches initially apply the ABSA methods as multi-label classification function. Finally, we review some emerging topics and discuss some open challenges to outlook potential future directions of ABSA. © 2023 Author(s).},
