	abstract = {It is recorded that timely diagnosis of disease like cancer improves survival rate and treatment procedure. Machine learning based models are showing the most promising results in cancer prediction, survivability analysis, and helping doctors in making informed decisions on treatment. With the advancements in imaging techniques, Feature selection and Classification on these images using deep neural network is showing promising results in diagnosis process, treatment selection and personalized medicines. These Machine Learning and Deep Learning based models are helping oncologists in making appropriate decisions thereby improving survivability and life expectancy of cancer patients. Application of CNN for deep feature extraction and classification has more promising results as compared to traditional machine learning algorithms. In this study we have looked at the various techniques used in prediction of cancer, identification of cancer stages and classification of tumors as malignant or benign. Broadly the methodologies can be classified into the following categories: (i) Feature extraction from CT/PET(Positron Emission Tomography)/HSI(Hyper spectral Images)/MRI/US (Ultrasound)/CLE (Confocal Laser Endomicroscopy) images using Radiomics and then apply traditional Machine Learning algorithms like SVM, Decision tree, KNN, Random Forest, MLP, Naïve Bayes (ii) applying specific Deep Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) Architectures along with Adaptive learning and Transfer learning and (iii) applying CNN to extract features followed by traditional machine learning algorithms for tumor classification. We have analyzed and compared the classification accuracy of different types of head and neck cancer Prediction models built with aforesaid methodologies and varied datasets and proposed future research direction for improving the accuracy. © 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.},
