	affiliations = {Dr. Rammanohar Lohia Avadh University, Institute of Engineering and Technology, Department of Information and Technology, U.P., Ayodhya, India},
	abstract = {Machine learning approaches for lung respiratory sound identification and categorization have increased in study. Transfer learning uses pre-trained models to extract relevant attributes from input data, one of the most promising strategies for high accuracy in this activity. In this review, many transfer learning algorithms for lung breathing sound identification are described. First, discuss respiratory sounds and their clinical significance. Next discuss the challenges of recognizing these sounds, such as the vast variety of sound characteristics and the requirement for trustworthy feature extraction techniques. Next, examine transfer learning methods such fine-tuning pre-trained convolutional neural networks (CNNs), learning from comparable tasks, and unsupervised pre-training. Focusing on current research on lung respiratory sound identification. Also compare each method's benefits and limitations. The discussion finishes with the field's most urgent difficulties, including the need for bigger and more diversified datasets, enhanced feature extraction techniques, and clinical information in machine learning models. In conclusion, this research examines the latest transfer learning algorithms for lung breathing sound recognition. It emphasizes these technologies potential to improve clinical diagnostic accuracy and efficiency and recommends numerous interesting research opportunities.  © 2023 IEEE.},
