	abstract = {Agriculture holds a vital role in India's economy, with a significant portion of its population reliant on this sector. The success of agricultural production is influenced by environmental factors beyond human control, such as weather conditions. Disease, however, is a controllable parameter that can impact crop productivity and quality. Proper disease management is essential to enhance crop output and reduce the need for harmful pesticides. Among the essential crops, cauliflower has gained prominence in India due to its nutritional value and economic benefits. However, the application of pesticides on cauliflower poses health risks, emphasizing the need for early disease detection. For many years, scientists have researched how to deal with the common diseases of Cauliflower is susceptible to various diseases, with researchers primarily focusing on white rust, black rot, bacterial soft rot and downy mildew. However, there are still many diseases and parts of Cauliflower have not been completed. This paper conducts a comprehensive survey and analysis of disease classification and detection techniques specifically applied to identify cauliflower diseases. The paper evaluates the strengths and limitations of the proposed methodologies. We talk about how diseases in plants are automatically detected by using machine learning and deep learning. Our investigation places a particular emphasis on the recent developments in deep learning methodologies over the past five years. Additionally, we provide an in-depth analysis of various datasets pertaining to plant diseases. Our objective is to clarify the details about the diseases and how to detect them promptly with machine learning, deep learning and CNN technologies. © 2023 IEEE.},
