	affiliations = {Faculty of Sciences and Techniques, Computer, Systems and Telecommunications Laboratory, Tangier, Morocco},
	abstract = {According to the most recent global cancer statistics from WHO, cancer is considered one of the most severe diseases and is becoming one of the main reasons for human deaths globally. Skin cancer is the greater popular kind in view of prolonged exposure to the sun's harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation. In order to minimize the severity of this disease, since it is more curable in the early stages, initial detection is ideal. Given the importance of this challenge, recently, using artificial intelligence techniques, researchers have developed various methods for early skin cancer lesions, which have been effectively used in the detection, classification, and treatment of various classes of skin diseases, and helping dermatologists in early diagnosis, and thus increasing the patient’s chance of recovery quickly. We present in this paper the latest research article’s details for detecting and classifying skin cancer using AI methods. In this context, we examined more than 100 publications from the last five years and we discussed and analyzed the advancements in AI solutions that exist to aid dermatologists and improve their capacity to detect skin cancer. Additionally, we give a summary of the most popular (deep and machine) learning models and datasets used for training. In this work, we concentrated on doing a comprehensive comparison of different works related to the utilization of AI techniques for skin cancer identification and categorizing is provided. © 2023 SPIE.},
