	abstract = {The selection and tuning of feature selection, feature engineering, and classification or regression algorithms is a major challenge in machine learning, affecting both beginners and experts. Automated machine learning (AutoML) offers a solution by automating the creation of machine learning pipelines, eliminating the guesswork associated with a manual process. This chapter reviews the challenges of building pipelines and introduces some of the most widely used AutoML methods and open-source software. We focus on TPOT, an AutoML method that utilizes genetic programming for discovery and optimization and represents pipelines as expression trees. We also explore TPOT extensions and its use in handling biomedical big data. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2023. All rights reserved.},
