	abstract = {The count of heart disease is increasing in India day by day. A lot of people die because of this disease without taking any medical treatment. The reason is there is no early symptoms or indication in patients. This makes it of extreme importance to predict not only myocardial Infarction (MI) but early MI also. In this research, the detection of myocardial infarction using an actual dataset is proposed. In this research, the dataset is categorized as angina (Early MI), MI, and NON-MI. Here consciously expertise opinion is taken and an actual dataset is collected from the hospitals. Input features are selected with the help of a literature survey and questionnaire circulated among the doctors. A new feature selection path is proposed. Based on these features the datasets are gathered from various hospitals. This dataset isn't adequate to give to the model. Provided that limited information restricts the training of the model subsequent in conceded results. To overawed the difficulty, an additional path is to be taken by providing synthetic data so as to supply information in a large to the model. A very novel idea transfer learning is useful in this study to get improved accuracy of the model. Supervised algorithms of machine learning such as Support Vector Machine (SVM), Naïve Bayes (NB), Decision Tree (DT), Random Forest (RF), K-Nearest Network (KNN), Quadratic discriminant analysis (QDA), AdaBoost are trained and tested on synthetic as well on actual datasets. An ensemble algorithm is applied to actual datasets to enhance the accuracy of the model.  © 2022 IEEE.},
