	abstract = {The scientific and engineering communities are increasingly turning to machine learning methods to make predictions of the physical properties of unknown systems. These methods, together with established statistical analyses, present practitioners with a varied property prediction toolbox. In this chapter, we review applications of property prediction in product formulation projects. We use these applications to discuss reasonable expectations and special considerations when using machine learning in formulation property prediction. Then, we introduce and evaluate both common and advanced machine learning methods that can be used in those projects, including random forests, neural networks, support vector machines, and transfer learning. We conclude with a synthetic worked example to demonstrate a concrete approach to beginning and then refining machine learning models. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Alix Schmidt and Kristin Wallace. All rights reserved.},
