	abstract = {Human activity recognition (HAR) is a research area focused on identifying the type of activity performed by an individual with the purpose of supporting the management of chronic diseases and promoting healthy lifestyle. HAR techniques analyze data collected by sensing devices and have motivated the development of various health-tracking applications. The integration of ICT and sensor technology has enabled this field to flourish beyond unfathomable levels. Many HAR-related reviews have been published in the literature; however, compared with other reviews, this chapter aims to provide a broader mapping of HAR techniques, including deep learning, machine learning, ensembled learning, metaheuristic algorithms, transfer learning, and reinforcement learning. It categorizes HAR techniques as data collection, data preprocessing, feature engineering, and model development. It identifies the benefits and drawbacks of each technique in each category. Finally, various challenges associated with these techniques as well as the future scope of research are discussed. © 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.},
