	affiliations = {Yashwantrao Chavan College of Engg, Department Of Computer Technology, Maharashtra, Nagpur, India; Yashwantrao Chavan College of Engg, Dept of Information Technology, Maharashtra, Nagpur, India},
	abstract = {Throat cancer is a disease state in which a malignant growth occurs at the pharynx, larynx, or tonsils. The current methods of diagnosis have much room for improvement. The traditional techniques are based strongly on invasive procedures and are highly handicapped by their subjectivity and the inherent intra- and interobserver variability in the clinical interpretation of the operations. This paper looks at existing models of advanced throat cancer detection using multimodal analysis coupled with machine- learning techniques. This review includes state-of-the-art techniques: Convolutional Neural Networks, Recurrent Neural Networks, and hybrid models combining CNNs and RNNs with other machine learning methods. By learning from multiple modes of collected information, such as medical imaging data, genome data, and records of patient health, the series of models created can be data-driven in the furthering of diagnostic accuracy. Key methodologies analyzed include CNN-Based Imaging Analysis, applied due to their capability to automatically extract and learn features from medical images, thus increasingly improving the precision of the diagnosis, together with a reduction of the involvement of manual intervention operations. RNNs for Temporal Data, which have applications to sequential data analysis of patient records, capturing temporal dependencies, all crucial elements in disease progression and understanding. In addition, this work further examines the possible ways transfer learning, as well as ensemble learning, can help boost model performance. This work's impact is rather significant in a way that it shows how multimodal analysis and machine learning can be pivotal in their role toward throat cancer detection. Improved capacities in reviewed models regarding early diagnosis, in turn, may improve earlier discovery of the patients and consequently survival rates, while minimization of treatment costs occurs.  © 2024 IEEE.},
