	abstract = {The early identification of brain diseases is important for prompt clinical intervention and effective treatment. Manual detection of brain tumors is complex and heavily reliant on specialized expertise. With the emergence of new brain diseases, the variability among these conditions poses a significant challenge for current diagnostic systems, making it a continuing focus of research. Detecting brain diseases promptly greatly impacts treatment success. The rise of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in neurology has revolutionized disease prediction and detection accuracy. This review delves into present growths in Deep learning (DL) and Machine learning (ML) approaches specifically aimed at the detection of brain tumors. It examines numerous studies that employ diverse techniques, modalities, and datasets. The overview provides a comprehensive look at the range of techniques utilized in diagnosing brain diseases. Summarizing important results from these studies, it addresses significant issues concerning ML and Deep Learning methods for diagnosing brain diseases. The ultimate goal is to pinpoint the maximum precise method for detecting a variety of brain diseases, thereby paving the way for future advancements in diagnosis and treatment. © 2024 IEEE.},
