	affiliations = {Data Science Coimbatore Institute of Technology, Department of Computing, Tamil Nadu, Coimbatore, India},
	abstract = {The proposed methodology uses Artificial Neural Networks (ANN) to predict stress levels of women working in educational institutions by analyzing physiological and demographic data collected through wearable technology. TensorFlow Federated framework is used here to ensure the data privacy by enabling secure and decentralized training of the proposed model. The approach integrates various steps, including data preprocessing, feature selection, and model training with federated learning. Based on predicted stress levels, the platform provides personalized recommendations to manage stress and improve mental well-being, while keeping user data private. The process involves collecting data from surveys and wearable devices, optimizing the model through techniques like hyperparameter tuning and regularization, and deploying the system via a web interface for real-time stress management. © 2024 IEEE.},
