	abstract = {The 2019 Coronavirus disease pandemic and its repercussions have been felt all around the globe. Shifting market forces made online shopping, an already powerful aspect of recent years economy, even more prevalent. Now more than ever, there are incentives to be competitive and please clients. One of the mechanisms put in place to keep track of such satisfactions are review scores. In this work we will explore an online shopping and reviews dataset, trying to predict customer satisfaction based on features related to the client, order details, among others, using machine learning techniques such as linear discriminant analysis and deep learning. The main contributions of this work are providing improvements on the currently used approaches, by generating new features from geolocation variables such as shipping distance, and by using ensembles of different classification techniques. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2023.},
