	journal = {Data Science with Semantic Technologies: New Trends and Future Developments},
	pages = {145 – 172},
	doi = {10.1201/9781003310785-8},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85190488773&doi=10.1201%2f9781003310785-8&partnerID=40&md5=dfc3a6013eed0a77b174f5679407fe0c},
	affiliations = {School of Computer Science and Engineering, Vellore Institute of Technology, AP University, Amaravathi, India; Vellore Institute of Technology, AP University, Amaravathi, India; School of Computer Science and Engineering, Vellore Institute of Technology, AP University, Amaravati, India},
	abstract = {As a civilization, we gather so much data, however, we do so little efficiently with it. Super stores gather data regarding customer transactions, provide financial accounts, and report distribution difficulties. Hospitals conduct tests and hold patient data records. Moreover, financial organizations also provide records of potential clients and gather statistics of existing client performances. Market surveys, traffic behavior, and product performance are documented to improve performance and management decisions. Machine learning (ML) is applied to these areas due to its capability of learning from data and improving themselves accordingly. In this chapter, a brief description about the future directions of telecommunications, hyperautomation, and autoML in health care will be discussed. Summary of future trends of machine learning: Telecommunications: With the emergence of 5G technology in telecommunications, many devices will increase the network traffic load. In order to offer seamless integration with all devices connected with a network, ML methods can be applied with the Internet-of-Things (IoT) to attain the best possible outcomes. Hyper automation: Hyper automation will take things a step further by adding a layer of “artificial brain” to the process, making it even smarter beyond automated processes. Hyper automation requires the selection of the right data/tool and an ML algorithm that lets bots identify the right patterns in data to develop insights from pattern recognition. AutoML in healthcare: Automated machine learning (AutoML) provides methods that non-machine learning experts can access easily. AutoML can help healthcare professionals with limited data science expertise better utilize machine learning models. © 2023 CRC Press.},
