	affiliations = {PetroChina Southwest Oil and Gasfield Company, China; SLB, United States},
	abstract = {In this case study we present the successful application of an automated machine learning first-break picking workflow to an onshore seismic survey from the Sichuan basin in China. We provide an overview of the main steps of this workflow from training data selection through to the various machine learning model architectures employed and demonstrate the uplift in both the resulting reservoir imaging and the reduction in the time taken to achieve these results. The application of the refraction statics, derived from the machine learning picks output from this workflow, provided improvements in event continuity at the common midpoint stack level and enabled the reduction in the amount of required human interpretation resulting in a shorter cycle time for this task when compared against the conventional iterative human intensive approach routinely used within the industry. © 2024 Society of Exploration Geophysicists and the American Association of Petroleum Geologists.},
