	affiliations = {Big Data Analytics and Web Intelligence Laboratory, Department of Computer Science, Delhi Technological University, New Delhi, India},
	abstract = {The ability to spot false news is becoming increasingly important in today’s environment. Modern, rapid communication and easy access to all kinds of information were made possible by social networks and internet media. On the other hand, it opens up new avenues for malicious people to exploit vast amounts of publicly available data. Fake images and videos may now be predicted with greater accuracy because of advances in machine learning, particularly deep learning. Many studies have been conducted in recent years to better understand how deepfakes work, and several deep learning-based algorithms to detect deepfake videos or images have been developed. This study provides a comprehensive summary of the most recent manipulation techniques and datasets utilized in this subject. In addition, we reviewed the recent work of other academics on the subject and provided a roadmap for future study to aid scholars in combating the issue of deep fakes. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd 2023.},
